      "lines": [
        {
          "line": 1,
          "text": "# Literal invocation environment"
        },
        {
          "line": 2,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 3,
          "text": "`CommandInvokeOptions.replaceEnv?: boolean` is additive. Absent or false retains"
        },
        {
          "line": 4,
          "text": "the runtime's existing environment merge behavior and PWD treatment. True uses"
        },
        {
          "line": 5,
          "text": "a fresh copy of exactly `options.env ?? {}` as the exported environment at"
        },
        {
          "line": 6,
          "text": "command entry: no merge with inherited exports, implicit PWD or promotion of"
        },
        {
          "line": 7,
          "text": "unexported/local variables. Supplied PWD is an environment value, not a cwd setter."
        },
        {
          "line": 8,
          "text": "Environment key/value validation remains required before child execution."
        },
        {
          "line": 9,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 10,
          "text": "This replaces the child environment, not generic shell state. Parent values,"
        },
        {
          "line": 11,
          "text": "export attributes and function locals must remain unchanged on success, error"
        },
        {
          "line": 12,
          "text": "or cancellation. Cwd resolution remains independent. A child Bash interpreter's"
        },
        {
          "line": 13,
          "text": "own initialization is separate from the environment passed to it."
        },
        {
          "line": 14,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 15,
          "text": "Literal argv, middleware, shared execution/output/depth budgets, signal,"
        },
        {
          "line": 16,
          "text": "stdout/stderr transfer and stdin cursor/origin rules are unchanged. Do not"
        },
        {
          "line": 17,
          "text": "implement replacement with a new Shell, new budget or a callback-only bypass."
        },
        {
          "line": 18,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 19,
          "text": "Core `env COMMAND` explicitly requests replacement for its already-computed"
        },
        {
          "line": 20,
          "text": "environment, including plain assignments and `-u`, not just `-i`. With no invoke"
        },
        {
          "line": 21,
          "text": "hook, its existing registry/callback fallback still receives that exact map."
        },
        {
          "line": 22,
          "text": "Generic directExecutor/xargs/find callers retain their existing default behavior."
        },
        {
          "line": 23,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 24,
          "text": "Curie owns the contract/core consumer; Sagan owns runtime/types. The additive"
        },
        {
          "line": 25,
          "text": "field and boundary-forwarding tests do not establish runtime support. Acceptance"
        },
        {
          "line": 26,
          "text": "requires the actual-shell nested env row and export/local/parent/cancellation"
        },
        {
          "line": 27,
          "text": "regressions after both implementations are committed. Preserve the historical"
        },
        {
          "line": 28,
          "text": "leak reproduction and original six-row cohort."
        },
        {
          "line": 29,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 30,
          "text": "# Cooperative invocation cleanup"
        },
        {
          "line": 31,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 32,
          "text": "```ts"
        }
      ]
